WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.161
- What was it like reading
the series finale script?

00:00:03.161 --> 00:00:06.180
(gentle ambient music)
(letters clacking)

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.770
- I don't know if there's a word

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.780
or even phrase that can sum it up.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.920
- It was like, "What the fuck?"

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.900
- My mom's gonna lose her mind.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.120
- I was shocked, scared for a lot of it.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.530
- I think the fans are gonna love it.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.780
- It's heartwarming, a little dangerous.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.250
- It's a big episode.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.420
- It's a rollercoaster.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.990
- A redemption for the
characters in the story.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.850
- There are deaths, there's heartache.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.140
- It's a crazy episode.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.420
Angelina gets her just desserts.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.500
- I have a lot to tell you.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.240
- But there's also tons of joy.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.400
- I don't think fans will
be disappointed at all.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.400
But for us as actors, it
was severely emotional.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.900
I mean, we're saying goodbye to characters

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.940
that we've held dear for so long.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.020
- That almost destroyed me.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.120
- I mean, this has been almost
five years of our lives.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.270
- I can't believe that this is the end.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.720
- I think it's the right
ending for these characters.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.700
And I cried a lot.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.480
- We've had most of the bones
of the finale in our head

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.830
from the very beginning.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:02.250
To finally put it on paper
was incredibly cathartic.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.460
The good people live, the bad people die,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.770
and everybody gets a do over.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.650
- It just feels right, so
when you're reading it,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.060
it doesn't feel like, "Wait, what?"

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.890
It kind of feels like, "Of course."

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.960
- I don't think I was surprised,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.864
I was more of just like,
"Yeah, it makes sense."

00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:23.520
- [Director] And action!

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.980
- We actually just finished
shooting a lot of it,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.440
and so going through
the acting aspect of it,

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.780
it just felt peaceful, it just felt right,

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.310
like a proper goodbye.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.950
- Catharsis, like a journey has completed.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.660
- But I don't wanna say goodbye.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.070
Why do I have to say goodbye?

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.930
- It's like a journey has ended,

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.310
but a new one is just starting.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.320
- Hmm, nice.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.880
- Oh my God.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.713
In Gupta's lab,

00:01:45.713 --> 00:01:48.210
they were tracking underwater
volcanoes across the globe.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.490
They had no way of tracking
subterranean volcanoes

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.480
that would arise on land.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.770
- You know, I play a scientist,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.470
so all the science stuff,
it can get very dense.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.330
- What's that line that you
have to say, "To procure-"

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.830
- Failed to procure a preferred grade

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.210
used commercial sapphire.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.530
- We're all gonna get that tattooed

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.480
on our bodies at some point.
- Absolutely, yes.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.090
- I was like, a little nervous
to shoot this final episode,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.960
because my character explodes.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.400
And when I was reading this script,

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.860
it says like, all the
other characters explode,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.510
and as I was reading it,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.980
I was like, "Thank God that's not me,"

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.847
and then it got to
Angelina and it was like,

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:21.097
"Angelina starts cracking and exploding

00:02:21.097 --> 00:02:23.160
"worse than all the others."

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.654
And I was like, "God damn it."

00:02:25.654 --> 00:02:27.690
Like, I also was just like, a little sad.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.010
I knew it was gonna be over.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.110
So yeah, it was a tough episode to shoot,

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.490
but I think very worth it.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.530
- I had a blast, 'cause in my real life,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.450
I have zero authority, you know?

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.790
And I've always wanted to play a character

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.240
who I get to get out of
a car, slam the door,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.120
and say something definitive
and then people follow me.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.490
- I don't need to tell
you that's impossible.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.760
- I did know after episode
10 that I would be back.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.750
I had lunch with Jeff back
in November of last year

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.490
before we started shooting season four.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.890
And he told me about everything,

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.990
because at the end of the first block,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.340
we know what happens to Zeke.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.440
But I knew that there would be a way

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.810
for Zeke to continue to be in the show

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.670
and to play an important role in it.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.120
And so I love the stuff that
I've had in season four.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.380
It feels like a little bit of a return

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.000
to season one and two for Zeke,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.310
which was like a dream come true for me.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.870
So yes, I knew.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.070
- I think they did a beautiful job

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.000
at bringing it all together.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:21.990
- Cal.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.040
- How'd you know my name?

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.770
- [Actor] You see a lot of
familiar people in this episode.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.190
- We see characters
from the very beginning

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.380
and we all come back together.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.470
- A lot of our storylines
don't always overlap,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.440
and so that's always fun
when the whole cast is in,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.430
because it's like a party.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.810
- It was like going to some kind

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.240
of strange high school reunion

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.580
where you see all these
people from your past.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.070
- A lot of giggles, a lot of crying,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.920
a lot of, "I don't wanna
do this right now."

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.970
- So to have us all together
again was, it was a lot of fun.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.400
- Michaela and I? We're
meant to be together.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.300
- Maybe, maybe not.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.010
- All these things that
have been talked about

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.860
and planted in stories
that have maybe gone away

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.910
are now coming back,

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.040
and that is a huge payoff for the fans.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.990
The fans of Zekaela, obviously,

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.930
we have these two factions
of really passionate people,

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.230
but I think the finale really
does service both groups.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.063
- A hundred percent.

00:04:14.063 --> 00:04:16.080
- And I hope that it really touches them.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.020
- One of the biggest, if not
the biggest disappointments

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.160
when we were canceled

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.880
was to not be able to finish
the story for the fans.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.140
That was a punch in the gut.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.930
And so when we were saved by Netflix

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.490
and to be able to share that-

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.260
- I think we might have
just saved the world.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.750
- We're coming back, we're
gonna finish the story,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.610
that was incredibly gratifying.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.630
- Thank you to Netflix.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.020
We now globally have a humongous audience

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.540
that are gonna be able
to enjoy this journey

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.640
because we now have this platform

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.500
to release all of four seasons.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.530
And this journey is ending,
but for a lot of people,

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.840
the journey is just beginning with Netflix

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.560
and being able to join us
on this "Manifest" ride.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.393
- Yeah.

00:04:56.393 --> 00:04:59.079
(dramatic music)

